    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Chef Barinov sits comfortably at the kitchen table and calmly drinks a cup of hot tea while complete chaos unfolds around him. Igor Valentinovich slowly approaches the chef, clearly annoyed by the man's relaxed behavior in the middle of a busy workday.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Что здесь происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы просто работаем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "На кухне полный хаос.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "А вы сидите здесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Чайком балуемся, Виктор Петрович?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, чай очень вкусный.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я люблю отдыхать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это правильно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Вы должны работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мои повара всё знают.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Они работают за меня.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Это просто возмутительно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Не кричите на меня.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Let us break down this interaction.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Чайком балуемся, Виктор Петрович?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Having some tea, Viktor Petrovich?' Russian leaves out 'am', 'is', or 'are' in the present tense, linking 'tea' straight to 'Petrovich'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это правильно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'That is right.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'this' with 'right'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "igor",
      "t": "Вы должны работать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You must work.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'you' with 'to work'.",
